{"text":"kuruntokai","n":20,"lines":["அருளும் அன்பும் நீக்கித் துணைதுறந்து","பொருள்வயிற் பிரிவோர் உரவோர் ஆயின்","உரவோர் உரவோர் ஆக","மடவம் ஆக மடந்தை நாமே"],"tr":["aruḷum aṉpum nīkkit tuṇaituṟantu","poruḷvayiṟ pirivōr uravōr āyiṉ","uravōr uravōr āka","maṭavam āka maṭantai nāmē"],"colophon":{"tinai":"pālai","tinai_ta":"பாலை","speaker_ta":"தலைவி கூற்று","poet_ta":"கோப்பெருஞ்சோழன்","speaker_en":"the heroine (talaivi)","poet_tr":"Kōpperuñcōḻaṉ"},"scan":{"meter":"nēricai āciriyappā","ok":true,"checks":[{"name":"lines","ok":true,"detail":"4 lines"},{"name":"feet per line","ok":true,"detail":"3×4, 1×3 feet"},{"name":"foot types","ok":true,"detail":"iyaṟcīr 14, veṇcīr 1"},{"name":"linkage","ok":true,"detail":"āciriyattaḷai 7, veṇṭaḷai 6, kalittaḷai 1"},{"name":"ending","ok":true,"detail":"ends on ஏ"}],"ending":"ஏ","lines":[[{"text":"அருளும்","tr":"aruḷum","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"அரு","tr":"aru"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ளும்","tr":"ḷum"}]},{"text":"அன்பும்","tr":"aṉpum","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"அன்","tr":"aṉ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"பும்","tr":"pum"}]},{"text":"நீக்கித்","tr":"nīkkit","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"நீக்","tr":"nīk"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கித்","tr":"kit"}]},{"text":"துணைதுறந்து","tr":"tuṇaituṟantu","foot":"karuviḷaṅkāy","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"துணை","tr":"tuṇai"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"துறந்","tr":"tuṟan"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"து","tr":"tu"}]}],[{"text":"பொருள்வயிற்","tr":"poruḷvayiṟ","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"பொருள்","tr":"poruḷ"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"வயிற்","tr":"vayiṟ"}]},{"text":"பிரிவோர்","tr":"pirivōr","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"பிரி","tr":"piri"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வோர்","tr":"vōr"}]},{"text":"உரவோர்","tr":"uravōr","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"உர","tr":"ura"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வோர்","tr":"vōr"}]},{"text":"ஆயின்","tr":"āyiṉ","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"ஆ","tr":"ā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யின்","tr":"yiṉ"}]}],[{"text":"உரவோர்","tr":"uravōr","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"உர","tr":"ura"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வோர்","tr":"vōr"}]},{"text":"உரவோர்","tr":"uravōr","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"உர","tr":"ura"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வோர்","tr":"vōr"}]},{"text":"ஆக","tr":"āka","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"ஆ","tr":"ā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"க","tr":"ka"}]}],[{"text":"மடவம்","tr":"maṭavam","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"மட","tr":"maṭa"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வம்","tr":"vam"}]},{"text":"ஆக","tr":"āka","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"ஆ","tr":"ā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"க","tr":"ka"}]},{"text":"மடந்தை","tr":"maṭantai","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"மடந்","tr":"maṭan"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"தை","tr":"tai"}]},{"text":"நாமே","tr":"nāmē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"நா","tr":"nā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"மே","tr":"mē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"அருளும்","parts":[{"text":"அருள்","lemma":"aruḷ","gloss":"compassion"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"compassion and"},{"surface":"அன்பும்","parts":[{"text":"அன்பு","lemma":"aṉpu","gloss":"love"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"love and"},{"surface":"நீக்கி","parts":[{"text":"நீக்கு","lemma":"nīkku","gloss":"to discard"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"having done"}],"gloss":"having discarded"},{"surface":"துணை","parts":[{"text":"துணை","lemma":"tuṇai","gloss":"companion"}],"gloss":"companion"},{"surface":"துறந்து","parts":[{"text":"துறந்து","lemma":"துறந்து","gloss":"having abandoned"}],"gloss":"having abandoned","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பொருள்வயின்","parts":[{"text":"பொருள்","lemma":"poruḷ","gloss":"wealth"},{"text":"வயின்","lemma":"vayiṉ","gloss":"for the sake of"}],"gloss":"for the sake of wealth"},{"surface":"பிரிவோர்","parts":[{"text":"பிரி","lemma":"piri","gloss":"to separate"},{"text":"வ்","lemma":"v","gloss":"future marker"},{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"they who"}],"gloss":"those who separate"},{"surface":"உரவோர்","parts":[{"text":"உரவோர்","lemma":"உரவோர்","gloss":"strong ones"}],"gloss":"strong ones","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஆயின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"āyiṉ","gloss":"if they are"}],"gloss":"if they are"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உரவோர்","parts":[{"text":"உரவோர்","lemma":"உரவோர்","gloss":"strong ones"}],"gloss":"strong ones","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"உரவோர்","parts":[{"text":"உரவோர்","lemma":"உரவோர்","gloss":"strong ones"}],"gloss":"strong ones","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஆக","parts":[{"text":"ஆகு","lemma":"āku","gloss":"to be"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"let"}],"gloss":"let them be"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மடவம்","parts":[{"text":"மடவம்","lemma":"மடவம்","gloss":"we are simple"}],"gloss":"we are simple","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஆக","parts":[{"text":"ஆகு","lemma":"āku","gloss":"to be"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"let"}],"gloss":"let us be"},{"surface":"மடந்தை","parts":[{"text":"மடந்தை","lemma":"maṭantai","gloss":"woman"}],"gloss":"woman"},{"surface":"நாமே","parts":[{"text":"நாம்","lemma":"nām","gloss":"we"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"we indeed"}]}],"literal":"Compassion and love having discarded, companion having abandoned, / for the sake of wealth those who separate, strong ones if they are, / let the strong ones be the strong ones; / let us be simple, we women indeed!","translation":"If those who abandon their companion, casting aside grace and love, to depart in search of wealth are considered strong-willed, then let those strong-willed men remain strong-willed. As for us, simple women, let us remain simple.","modern":"அருளையும் அன்பையும் நீக்கிவிட்டு, தன் துணையைத் துறந்து, பொருளின் பொருட்டுப் பிரிந்து செல்பவர்கள் வலிமை உடையவர்கள் என்றால், அந்த வலிமை உடையவர்கள் வலிமை உடையவர்களாகவே இருக்கட்டும். பெண்ணாகிய நாம் அறியாமை உடையவர்களாகவே இருப்போம்.","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the heroine to her confidante when the hero has left her to acquire wealth. It belongs to the Pālai tiṇai, which depicts the painful separation of lovers. The heroine uses gentle irony to cope with her grief, contrasting the 'strength' of the hero with her own 'simplicity'. If being strong-willed (uravōr) means having the coldness to abandon love and a partner for material gain, she declares that she has no desire for such strength. Instead, she and her companion are content to remain 'simple' or 'foolish' (maṭavam) women who value love above all else.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}